# Research notebook: two questions, one notebook
An agentic notebook written as .lnd. Each research task is a block, each finding keeps its source, each lesson is reusable memory, and each decision says how sure it is or abstains. One case is technical (search for a help center), one is not (a neighborhood bakery choosing a flour supplier). Example data; nothing here was measured.

// profile: lnd-1.1 · keys: en · scope: example · suggested_views: board, web, source

---

@source f-bakery-quotes
title: Three flour quotes received by the bakery, week 1
url: https://example.org/bakery/quotes
date: 2026-10-12
@@

@source f-bakery-tasting
title: Blind tasting of bread made with each flour, six regular customers
url: https://example.org/bakery/tasting
date: 2026-10-15
@@

@source f-search-trial
title: Trial of two search approaches on 40 real help-center questions
url: https://example.org/help/search-trial
date: 2026-10-16
@@

@task t-quotes
title: Ask three mills for a price and delivery quote
status: done
priority: high
owner: team
@@

@task t-tasting
title: Bake the same loaf with each flour and run a blind tasting
status: done
priority: high
depends_on: t-quotes
owner: team
@@

@task t-search-trial
title: Compare keyword search and meaning-based search on real questions
status: done
priority: medium
owner: team
@@

@task t-traffic
title: Collect one week of real traffic before choosing where the help center runs
status: pending
priority: medium
depends_on: d-hosting
owner: team
@@

@claim c-flour-b
text: Customers picked the bread made with flour B in four of six tastings.
source: f-bakery-tasting
certainty: Assumed
@@

@claim c-flour-delivery
text: Only mills A and B deliver twice a week; mill C delivers once.
source: f-bakery-quotes
certainty: Verified
@@

@claim c-search
text: Meaning-based search found the right article for 31 of 40 questions; keyword search found 24.
source: f-search-trial
certainty: Assumed
@@

@experience x-taste-blind
lesson: Run tastings blind and with regular customers; staff always prefer the flour they already know.
origin: @(c-flour-b)
applies_to: bakery, suppliers, tasting
uses: 1
status: Assumed
@@

@experience x-real-questions
lesson: Test search with questions people actually asked, not with questions the team wrote.
origin: @(c-search)
applies_to: search, help center
uses: 2
status: Verified
@@

@decision d-flour
question: Which mill supplies the bakery's flour from next month?
options: Mill A · Mill B · Mill C
criterion: Customers liked the bread | 3 | 3 | 4 | 3
criterion: Delivers twice a week | 2 | 5 | 5 | 1
criterion: Price per sack | 1 | 4 | 3 | 5
chosen: Mill B
candidates: Mill B · Mill A
confidence: 0.7
status: decided
date: 2026-10-18
source: @(c-flour-b) · @(c-flour-delivery)
reopen_if: two late deliveries in one month or customers start leaving bread on the plate
@@

@decision d-search
question: Which search does the help center use first?
options: Keyword search · Meaning-based search
candidates: Meaning-based search · Keyword search
chosen: Meaning-based search
confidence: 0.6
status: decided
date: 2026-10-19
source: @(c-search)
reopen_if: fewer than 70 of 100 real questions find the right article after one month
@@

@decision d-hosting
question: Where does the help center run?
options: Static host · Own server · Both
candidates: Static host · Own server
status: abstained
reopen_if: we have one week of real traffic numbers
@@
